<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Theognostus, Metropolitan of Kiev</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1353">1353</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Theognostus was a Greek churchman appointed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> as Metropolitan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kiev</a> and All Rus', an office he held from 1328 until his death in 1353. Succeeding Peter, he made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> his permanent residence, cooperated closely with Ivan I and his son Simeon, and secured the canonisation of his predecessor. His residence tied the head of the Rus' church to the rising Muscovite dynasty.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>…head of the Rus' church, settled in Moscow around 1325 and died there in 1326, and his successor <b>Theognostus</b> made the town his residence, giving the young dynasty a religious centre to add to the lucrative right, which came with the grand princely title, to collect the Horde's…</blockquote><a href="/empire/grand-duchy-of-moscow">Grand Duchy of Moscow · Foundation</a></li></ul></section>
